# Certificate Secret Configuration for Twitch Service
# DO NOT commit actual certificates to version control
#
# The twitch service reuses the existing auth-certs secret which contains public.pem.
# No separate certificate secret is needed for the twitch service.
#
# The auth-certs secret should already exist from the auth service deployment.
# If you need to create or update it, see k8s/auth/cert-secret.yaml.template
#
# The twitch service only needs public.pem (not private.pem) since it only
# verifies JWTs, doesn't sign them. The auth-certs secret contains both
# private.pem and public.pem, but the twitch service will only use public.pem
# from the mounted volume at /app/certs/public.pem.
#
# Note: The secret will be mounted as a volume in the deployment
# at the path specified by CERT_PATH in the ConfigMap (default: /app/certs)
#
# The deployment references auth-certs in the volume configuration:
#   volumes:
#   - name: certs
#     secret:
#       secretName: auth-certs

